"C-004": {
  "statement": "A multi-hop revolving-door detector (D11) \u2014 joining lobbyists whose covered_position text names a specific committee, current quarterly filings, and the issue-code those filings lobby on \u2014 surfaces a particularly dense cluster at Brownstein Hyatt Farber Schreck LLP: Russell Sullivan (former Staff Director, Senate Finance Committee) and Mark Warren (former Chief Tax Counsel, Senate Finance Committee; Senior Tax Counsel to Sen. Thune; Tax Counsel, House Ways & Means; Deputy Assistant Secretary, Treasury Legislative Affairs) both lobby Apollo Global Management, Athene Holding (Apollo's annuities arm), Johnson & Johnson Services, T-Mobile, Bloom Energy, and the American Petroleum Institute on TAX/FIN topics. Sullivan alone has appeared in 1,714 federal lobbying filings and lifetime-tracked revenue exceeding $76 million per OpenSecrets. The detector identified 16 named lobbyists representing $122 million in 2024-2026 lobbying income on topics directly aligned with the committee they previously staffed. **Bill-citation analysis confirms Brownstein Hyatt cited H.R. 1 (the 2025 'Big Beautiful Bill' tax-and-spending reconciliation) 256 times across its lobbying activities, and H.R. 5376 (Inflation Reduction Act) 37 times \u2014 the most-lobbied bills in the corpus by this single firm. Cross-corpus 'say vs. pay' signal: Sen. Elizabeth Warren issued ten 2024-2025 press releases publicly attacking Apollo Global Management over the Steward Health Care bankruptcy \u2014 while Sullivan + Warren billed the same Apollo $8.92M for representation during the same period.**",
